Subject: Research and goldfish output that misread live data or misled

Found in the gateway's live run of 2026-10-11 (Mystic Forge 1.3.2-mag2):

- edhrec_precon_upgrade printed "?%" for every card to add. EDHREC's precon
  pages now send num_decks with potential_decks (Tatyova, Benthic Druid: 969
  of 1612 for Reap the Tides) and no "inclusion". It also headed EDHREC's
  precon_commander_counts "Commanders in this precon", but that list holds
  every commander people built the precon around (Koma, Cosmos Serpent and
  twenty more); the precon's own commander is in the page's deck.commander.
- edhrec_salt printed "Stasis — " with nothing after the dash: the salt page
  now sends a numeric "salt" (3.06) and no "label".
- edhrec_top_cards printed each section's list without its heading, so the
  numbering restarted eight times with nothing to say why. With a colour the
  page is pages/top/<colour>.json, which has no time period (its counts are
  over all decks), so period was silently not used; the output now says so.
- edhrec_recommendations listed EDHREC's outRecs as "Consider Cutting",
  including cards that were never given (Wastes, Forest, Island for a list of
  one Sol Ring). Only cards from the given list are shown as cuts now.
- spellbook_card_combos printed "None total" when Commander Spellbook sends
  "count": null.
- precon_decklist and precon_export printed one line per MTGJSON printing
  ("8 Forest" and "7 Forest"); lines for the same card are added together.
- goldfish_annotate (and every goldfish tool) skipped double-faced cards
  given by their full name ("Enduring Angel // Angelic Enforcer", "Elbrus,
  the Binding Blade // Withengar Unbound"): Scryfall's collection lookup does
  not find the full name, only the front face. Lookups now use the front
  face; the card found keeps its full name. The pre-flight also says how many
  copies of an unrecognized name were skipped.
- The honesty report filed lands and mana rocks that were played (Island,
  Sol Ring, Arcane Signet) under "Modeled, low-impact ... only this group
  supports 'the sim agrees this card underperforms'", because they fire no
  trigger. Mana sources that were played are listed apart now
  (honesty.modeled_mana_sources), never as low-impact.
- on_curve.avg_lands_by_turn is the land drops made in each turn (the
  per-turn counter resets every turn), not lands in play; the report's chart
  called it "Average lands in play by turn". The chart is renamed and
  on_curve.avg_land_drops_by_turn carries the same numbers under a clear
  name (avg_lands_by_turn stays for existing readers).

Tests: tests/test_research_output_fixes.py; tests/goldfish/test_metrics.py
and tests/goldfish/test_report.py follow the new honesty key and chart title.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 (main, 2026-10-04) has none of
these fixes. Drop each part when upstream carries it.

